   "say": "He escaped jail with a wooden gun. Then one short drive doomed him.",
   "hook": "ONE DRIVE DOOMED HIM"
  },
  {
   "say": "This is part two. He fled Crown Point in the sheriff's own Ford, heading for Chicago."
  },
  {
   "say": "Somewhere on that road, he crossed from Indiana into Illinois.",
   "hook": "THE STATE LINE"
  },
  {
   "say": "Bank robbery wasn't a federal crime yet. But driving a stolen car across state lines was."
  },
  {
   "say": "A federal charge was filed over the sheriff's car. Now federal agents could hunt him anywhere."
  },
  {
   "say": "J. Edgar Hoover made him top priority. By June, he was called America's first Public Enemy Number One.",
   "hook": "PUBLIC ENEMY NO. 1"
  },
  {
   "say": "A $10,000 reward was offered. A Chicago brothel owner, Anna Sage, facing deportation, tipped off the agents."
  },
  {
   "say": "July 22, 1934. Dillinger walked out of the Biograph Theater after a Clark Gable gangster film.",
   "hook": "THE BIOGRAPH"
  },
  {
   "say": "Agents were waiting. He reached for his gun. They opened fire, and he died that night."
  },
  {
   "say": "His bank robberies made him famous. A stolen car across a state line is what brought him down."
  },
  {
   "say": "Genius escape, dumb getaway, or was he set up? Tell me in the comments.",
   "hook": "YOUR VERDICT"
  }
